PCP License 1.1 — Pure Cognition Pass Unified License

Copyright © 2025 PCPCODE
All Rights Reserved Except As Granted Below.

PCP stands for “Pure Cognition Pass”, representing a unified system of cognitive integrity and ethical usage.

0. Purpose

The PCP License establishes a non-commercial, ethical, threshold-based permission system that protects creator rights while enabling responsible learning, modification, and micro-commercial use.

1. Non-Commercial Use

You may freely use this work for personal, educational, artistic, research, or other non-commercial purposes.
No permission is required for non-commercial use.

2. Threshold Commercial Use (≤ 10 USD)

Commercial activity involving this work or any derivative is allowed only when:

Total accumulated revenue does not exceed 10 USD;

Ethical restrictions in Section 3 are respected;

Proper credit to “PCPCODE” is provided.

If accumulated revenue exceeds 10 USD, explicit written permission from the author is required.

3. Ethical Use Requirement (No Harmful Use)

This work may not be used for harmful, abusive, deceptive, malicious, or discriminatory purposes, including but not limited to:

Surveillance targeting individuals

Manipulation, exploitation, harassment

Political misinformation or propaganda

Fraud, cyberattacks, automated harm

Psychological manipulation systems

Discriminatory or abusive applications

The author reserves sole discretion to determine what constitutes “harmful use”.

4. Conditional Permission for Modifications

Modification or derivative works are permitted by default when:

The purpose is non-commercial, or revenue is within the ≤10 USD threshold;

Ethical restrictions are followed;

The original author is credited.

All other cases require explicit written permission.

5. Redistribution

Redistribution is permitted when:

It is non-commercial, or

Revenue is within the threshold, and

This license is included in full, and

Credit to “PCPCODE” is provided.

6. No Transfer of Rights

This license does not transfer ownership.
All intellectual property rights remain with the author.

7. No Warranty

This work is provided “as is” without warranty of any kind.
The author assumes no liability for damages or claims arising from its use.

8. Enforcement and Consequences of Violation

If any user violates this license:

All permissions are automatically and permanently terminated.

The violator must immediately cease all use, access, and distribution.

The violator must destroy all copies of the work and derivatives.

The violator is permanently banned from receiving future licenses.

The author may pursue legal remedies, including civil claims, injunctions, and damages.

Further use is prohibited unless the author grants new written permission.

9. Governing Principles

This license is guided by cognitive integrity, ethical responsibility, creator sovereignty, non-commercial fairness, and sustainable knowledge sharing.

